The new code hardcodes backtick quoting (`\`o_\``) instead of using `$db->quoteIdentifier()`. This is a **potential portability issue** — `quoteIdentifier()` would use the platform-specific identifier quoting (e.g., double quotes for PostgreSQL, brackets for MSSQL). Hardcoding backticks makes this MySQL/MariaDB-specific.

